   "status": "MISMATCH",
   "ruling": "Ruling: scope; the objection is a partial same-state overlap where both forms' column B would be counted and the overlapping months added twice, and the December-2025 marriage with separate plans. The project refuses both: f8962.two_counted asks whether two counted Forms 1095-A from one state show coverage in the same month and refuses lines 24 and 25 on Yes (i8962 p. 16, Column (b), \"Enter the amount from column B of only one Form 1095-A—do not add the amounts from each form.\"); f8962.marriage refuses a return married in 2025 with coverage before the first full month of marriage, which covers a December marriage. The ptc-sa package folded f8962.b_zero (a month with column (a) above zero and column (b) zero) into the same computed gate, so the gate now refuses more, never less. The render review of this collection form does not include the consuming form's gates.",
